title: Camera layouts
description: Switch a screen recording and the camera in front of it between corner, side-by-side, stacked and full-frame layouts as it plays.
---

import { Steps } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import AtAGlance from '@components/AtAGlance.astro';

A camera layout decides how a camera clip and the screen recording behind it share the frame. Choose one at any moment and the picture eases into it there, so a tutorial can go from a small corner camera to a full-frame 

<AtAGlance
  menu="Clip ▸ Camera Layout ▸"
  where="Clip tab ▸ Picture ▸ Layout"
  tools="switch_layout"
/>

## Switch the layout

<Steps>

1. Move the playhead to where the switch should start.

2. Tell Frame Job which clips to use. With nothing selected it looks for the track named "Camera", which is where a recording's camera lands, so usually there's nothing to do. Otherwise select the camera, or the camera a

3. Choose a layout from **Clip ▸ Camera Layout ▸**.

</Steps>

To change layout again later, move the playhead on and choose another. To undo a switch, press <kbd>⌘Z</kbd>: one undo step, **Camera Layout**, takes the whole switch back. These items have no keyboard shortcut.

